course: dictionary
lesson: 7423
title: Polish: shiny, or better
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Polish can be an action or a thing, so the words around it show you which meaning fits.
explain: «Polish the table until it shines.» Here polish is an action: rub something until it is smooth and shiny. «Use shoe polish on your school shoes.» Here polish is a thing: the cream or wax you rub on.
explain: Polish can also mean to make something better. «Polish your story» means check it and improve it, like tidying up a first draft. Always ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Polish (verb) means to rub something until it is smooth and shiny.
fact: Polish (noun) means a cream, liquid or wax used to make things shiny, such as «shoe polish» or «nail polish».
fact: «Polish off» means finish something quickly, and «polish up» means improve or refresh something.
fact: Polish with a capital P means from Poland, as in «a Polish pharmacist».
fact: Polish and nail polish remover are chemicals, so keep them away from small children and fire.
exercise: «Polish the silver until it shines.» What does polish mean here? | To eat something quickly | *To rub something until it is smooth and shiny | To hide something | A cream from Poland
exercise: «She put shoe polish on her boots.» What does polish mean here? | To finish a task quickly | A soft cloth | A person from Poland | *A cream or wax used to make things shiny
exercise: «Polish your story before you hand it in.» What does polish mean here? | To throw away | To rub with a cloth | *To improve something to make it better | To say it out loud
test: «A Polish pharmacist made a lamp in Lviv.» Why does Polish start with a capital P? | Because it starts a new paragraph | Because it means to rub | *Because it means from Poland | Because it is a shiny cream
test: «Polish off your lunch before the bell.» What does polish off mean? | Leave some food behind | *Finish quickly | Save it for later | Wash the plate
exam: «The shop sold a tin of polish and a new cloth.» What is polish here? | To finish a task quickly | A shiny stone | A person from Poland | *A cream or wax for making things shiny
